# BlackGust web (blackgust.uz)

Next.js 16 App Router + TypeScript, next-intl 4, GSAP + ScrollTrigger, Lenis. No Tailwind: one hand-written design system in `src/app/globals.css`.

## Read first
- Next.js 16 differs from older versions. Middleware is now `src/proxy.ts`. Check `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using an API you are unsure about.
- `params` in pages/layouts is a Promise: `const { locale } = await params`.

## Content & i18n
- ALL user-facing text lives in `src/messages/{uz,ru,en,zh,ko}.json`. `en.json` is the source of truth for keys; `uz` is the default locale.
- Never hardcode copy in components. Add the key to `en.json` and to every other locale, then run `npm run i18n:check` (must pass; it checks keys, array lengths, `{placeholders}` and link targets).
- Strings support inline markdown via `<Md>`: `[text](/path)`, `**bold**`, `*em*`. Internal links start with `/` and are locale-aware automatically.
- Prices are never written in messages. Use `{foundation}`, `{enterprise}`, `{sovereign}`, `{diagnostic}`, `{strategy}`, `{architecture}`, `{academy}`, `{advisory}`; values come from `src/config/site.ts` (USD everywhere) and are formatted by `src/lib/format.ts`.
- Headlines go through `<Split text=… />` so the GSAP word reveal works. `*word*` inside a headline renders as the lapis italic accent.
- Load page content on the server with `content(locale, "namespace")` from `src/lib/content.ts`.

## Contacts, prices, partner links
- Single source: `src/config/site.ts` (email, WhatsApp, phones, address, prices, parent company AISolution).

## Motion
- Global smooth scroll + header in `src/components/MotionRoot.tsx`.
- Page choreography in `src/lib/motion/page.ts`, started by `<PageMotion />` which MUST be the last element of every page (it runs after hydration; touching page DOM earlier breaks hydration).
- The live model on the home page: `src/lib/motion/flow.ts` (canvas engine, pure function of scroll progress + time) and `src/components/FlowViz.tsx` (markup + ScrollTrigger).
- Scroll scenes are opted in from markup: `data-scene="deck"` (cards dealt while pinned), `data-scene="checklist"` (items verified while pinned), `data-scrub` on a section (paragraph words light up on scroll). Pinned triggers are sorted by position before every refresh.
- Page transitions: `<PageTransition/>` (exit cover naming the destination) + the CSS shutter in `template.tsx` (entry). It dispatches `bg:leave` before `router.push` so `<PageMotion/>` unwraps pin spacers while the page still exists — never navigate programmatically from a page with pins without firing it.
- Globe hero: `src/lib/motion/globe.ts` via `<GlobeCanvas/>`. Intro (once per session) and the page shutter are pure CSS; everything is disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Content must be fully visible without JS and with `prefers-reduced-motion`. Only elements below the fold may be pre-hidden.
- Number formatting rendered on the server must be identical on the client (Intl differs between Node and browsers): always pass explicit `minimumFractionDigits`/`maximumFractionDigits`, and format through `numberTag(locale)` (uz ICU data is missing in some browsers).

## SEO
- Every page exports `generateMetadata` via `pageMetadata(locale, key, path)` — canonical + hreflang for all locales + OG.
- `/aisolution` is the parent-company page with a dofollow link to https://aisolution.uz (entity SEO). Keep it, and keep the footer "built by AISolution" line.
- JSON-LD: Organization + WebSite in the layout, FAQPage on /faq, ProfessionalService on /contact.

## Forms
- `src/app/api/lead/route.ts`: origin check, honeypot, min completion time, per-IP rate limit, duplicate suppression, optional Turnstile, delivery to Telegram and/or Resend. Never log personal data.

## Brand
- Colors are tokens in `:root` of globals.css. Lapis lazuli (`--lapis`, #5A8BE6 — Samarkand majolica blue) is the only accent; keep it under ~10% of any screen. Warning is orange (`--warn`), never lapis.
- Fonts: Spectral (display), IBM Plex Sans (body), IBM Plex Mono (labels) — self-hosted via @fontsource, no requests to Google.
